The revised module again passes every local gate. The structure-aware prior now samples uniformly from the full \((n-1)!\) permutations containing the required edge; it still produced 0/200,000 hits. All four attacks remain 0/8, canonicalization survives 80 composed relabellings, and the reference still solves 8/8 at about 8,069 lookups. I’m rerunning the bare oracle ladder on this corrected family; this intentionally overwrites the obsolete transcript from the leaked version.
